.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt KEXPORT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kexport
.Nd export a disk as a VM image, a container image or a Firecracker bundle
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar source
.Ar format
.Op Ar output-dir
.Op Fl -seal | Fl -no-seal
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
turns a disk \(em a machine's ZFS volume, a physical disk, or an image
file in any format
.Xr qemu-img 1
reads \(em into a file another platform can use:
.Bl -tag -width "firecracker"
.It Li qcow2
KVM, Proxmox, OpenStack; compressed.
.It Li raw
A plain disk image, sparse.
.It Li vhd
Azure and Hyper-V; fixed size.
.It Li vmdk
VMware ESXi and vSphere; stream-optimised.
.It Li ova
An OVF descriptor and a stream-optimised VMDK in one tar, for VMware and
VirtualBox.
.It Li oci
The root filesystem as a tar.gz for
.Ql docker import
or
.Ql podman import .
.It Li lxc
The root filesystem and a metadata tarball for
.Ql lxc-create -t local .
.It Li firecracker
The root filesystem as an ext4 image, the kernel found in its
.Pa /boot ,
a
.Pa config.json
and a
.Pa launch.sh ;
see
.Sx CAVEATS .
.It Li all
.Li qcow2 , raw , vhd , vmdk
and
.Li ova
in turn.
.El
.Pp
By default the output is sealed with
.Xr kldload-seal 8 :
the machine-id, ssh host keys, hostid, cloud-init state, logs and mesh
keys are removed, so every machine made from the image is a new one.
The seal is applied to a copy, and the source is never written:
.Bl -bullet
.It
a ZFS volume is snapshotted and cloned, which takes no time and no space;
the clone is sealed and exported, and it and the snapshot are removed at
the end.
A machine that is running can be exported this way: its disk is taken as
it is at that instant, as after a power cut;
.It
anything else is copied to a sparse raw file in
.Ar output-dir ,
which is sealed, exported and removed.
It needs room for what the disk holds.
.El
.Pp
The container formats and
.Li firecracker
mount the disk's largest partition, taken to be its root filesystem.
They too work from a clone of a ZFS volume, sealed or not; any other
source is mounted read-only, and refused while any of it is mounted on
this host.
.Pp
Output files are named
.Ar NAME Ns Pa \&. Ns Ar format ,
where
.Ar NAME
is
.Ev KEXPORT_NAME ,
or
.Ql kldload-export- Ns Ar YYYYMMDD-HHMM .
.Pp
It must run as root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar source
A block device, a ZFS volume
.Pq Pa /dev/zvol/ Ns Ar dataset ,
or an image file.
.It Ar format
One of the formats above.
.It Ar output-dir
Where the output goes; made if missing.
Default
.Pa /root/exports .
.It Fl -seal
Seal the copy; the default.
.It Fl -no-seal
Export the source as it is: the image keeps its identity, which suits
moving one machine, and does not suit making many.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KEXPORT_NAME
The output files' base name.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Exported.
.It 1
The source is not a disk or file, not root, a tool is missing, the seal
failed, or a conversion failed.
.It 2
A usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
