.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-29, writing this page:
the seal was applied to the source itself, so exporting a stopped machine
removed its identity and mesh keys for good;
every conversion treated the source as raw, so a qcow2 file was exported
as the bytes of its container;
the container formats could not work at all, the mount step's own log
line being captured as part of the mountpoint;
the OVF inside every OVA used an undeclared namespace prefix and was not
valid XML;
.Xr kldload-seal 8
could not seal an image file;
and the clone was removed without
.Fl r ,
which failed when the scheduled snapshots had taken one of it mid-export.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The OVA's descriptor is valid XML and names 4 processors and 4096 MB of
memory; it has not been imported into VMware or VirtualBox here.
.Pp
The Firecracker bundle carries the distribution's compressed kernel,
which Firecracker boots only from 1.17.0, and no initrd, which most
distribution kernels need to find their root disk; it has not been booted.
.Xr kfire 8
makes Firecracker machines that do.
.Pp
Only the largest partition is read for the container formats; a separate
.Pa /boot
or
.Pa /home
partition is not in the result.
.Pp
The
.Li vhd
format is fixed-size: the file is the disk's full size, sparse where the
filesystem allows.
.Pp
The fix for a clone snapshotted mid-export
.Pq Fl r
was not re-run against the scheduled snapshots.
